Z||000000||DreXteR||09-12-2001||04:52 PM||||Whic fan type is more effient, puller or pussher?  Regarding cooling, not air circulation or something else.<P>I beleive push is better, it perform the cooling by pushing air trough the fins.<P>Leave your imput.<P>Thanx<P>DreX||||reg||5
Z||000001||mrfixit58||09-12-2001||04:57 PM||||Puller. If for no other reason than the fact that the motor isn't in the way of the air flow. But the main reason is becauce you can us a shroud on a puller and draw air across a larger surface area with a smaller fan.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Roy  :D <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||DreXteR||09-12-2001||10:32 PM||||Iis not for the radiator. Is for an intercooler and will be placed in the lower quater panel, driver side. As can you imagine there will not be any kind of air directly to it. The air will just pass and the intercooler will not do its job. Thats why I will assists the intercooler with a electric fan.<P>DreX||||reg||1
Z||000003||Kasdan||09-12-2001||11:55 PM||||If i put electric fans under the vents, should they push or pull?<P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan<BR>1986 GT Fastback, <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FIERO2.JPG">       <BR>Holley Ram-Air, Power Steering, K&N Filtercharger, Bosch Wires, Bosch Platinum Plugs, Conrad Distribuiter Cap/Rotor, New GT Seats, New Headliner, New Carpet, Ocelet Exhaust, Red Underbody Light Kit (coming soon)<BR>Aim=FieroDriver1986||||reg||1
Z||000004||Leper||09-13-2001||12:35 AM||||Fans work best if they pull air.<BR>If you can't fit a fan behind the radiator/intercooler/oil cooler, then you have to put them in front and it doesn't matter if that's the best way or not.<BR>If you put fans under the vents, they should push the air out of the vents. The whole car is designed around air coming out through the top of the vents. The fans would be more efficient if they were pullers mounted on top of the vents, but that wold look stupid.||||reg||1
Z||000005||mrfixit58||09-13-2001||08:14 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Kasdan:<BR><B>If i put electric fans under the vents, should they push or pull?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>If your speaking about the grill above the motor on the rear deck, limited space may dictate you use pusher fans.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Roy  :D <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG">    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/halfpole.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Kasdan||09-13-2001||08:35 AM||||Pusher, like pushing into the compartment?<P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan, 1986 GT<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero21.jpg">         <BR>Power Steering, Holley Scoop<BR>Aim=FieroDriver1986||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||09-13-2001||07:30 PM||||Due to space constraints.... Aux Fans in the rear vent grates need to be configured for "push" and to blow up thru the grates.<P>Push means the air flows from the motor side of the fan. Pull is the way normal radiator fans work.<P>Space may also decide the intercooler fan. In general the fan makers prefer pull if posible. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||DreXteR||09-13-2001||09:27 PM||||theogre - The maximum size could be 7 1/2 in. The intercooler will be placed in lower quater panel, where the intake outside acces is placed. I will design or get some scoupes for there to improve airflow but will not be enough. Should I use the fan pulling or pushing??? If pushing the fan will be placed before the intercooler and if is pushing will be after. I dont beleive there will be enough air flow there to make the intercooler very eficient. <P>DreX||||reg||1
Z||000009||theogre||09-14-2001||07:41 PM||||In that small a space, I'm not sure the fan will make much dif either. You're also going to need air lines that are long and convoluted. That's likely going to increase boost lag considerably.||||reg||1
Z||000010||DreXteR||09-14-2001||10:51 PM||||Nop, my design is almost straigth.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>The lag will be minimal, will be equal or smallest than the intercooler cars.<P>DreX||||reg||12
